---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="How to Measure & Cut Crown Molding (Miter & Bevel Chart) | CalcForDIY"
  description="Master cutting crown molding flat on a compound miter saw or nested against the fence. Complete miter and bevel angle charts for 90° square and 135° bay window corners."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "How to Measure and Cut Crown Molding",
    "description": "Step-by-step master guide to measuring, calculating compound miter & bevel angles, and cutting crown molding.",
    "author": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "CalcForDIY Carpentry Division"
    },
    "publisher": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "CalcForDIY",
      "logo": {
        "@type": "ImageObject",
        "url": "https://calcfordiy.com/favicon.svg"
      }
    },
    "mainEntityOfPage": "https://calcfordiy.com/guides/how-to-cut-crown-molding"
  }
  </script>

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What angle do I cut crown molding for a 90 degree corner?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "For standard 52/38 degree crown molding laying flat on a compound miter saw table, set the miter angle to 31.62° and the bevel angle to 33.86°."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is the upside down and backwards method for crown molding?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "In the nested method, you place the top edge of the crown molding flat on the saw table and the bottom edge flat against the vertical fence (upside down). The saw blade stays at 0° bevel, and you cut with simple 45° miter angles."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>

  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4 print:hidden">
    <a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a>
    <span>/</span>
    <a href="/guides" class="hover:text-blue-600">Guides</a>
    <span>/</span>
    <span>How to Cut Crown Molding</span>
  </div>

  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-full text-blue-700 text-xs font-semibold mb-3">
        <span>🪵 Finish Carpentry Standards</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>Trade-Verified Spec Guide</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-3 tracking-tight">
        How to Measure &amp; Cut Crown Molding (Miter &amp; Bevel Angle Guide)
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
        Crown molding transforms a room, but cutting the corners intimidates many DIYers. Here is the exact compound angle reference and cut direction guide.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Quick Formula Box -->
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 border-2 border-blue-300 rounded-xl p-6 mb-8 shadow-xs">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-blue-950 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>📐</span> Quick Angle Chart for Standard 52/38&deg; Crown Molding (Flat Method):
      </h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm text-blue-900 mt-3">
        <div class="bg-white p-3 rounded-lg border border-blue-200">
          <strong>90&deg; Standard Inside/Outside Corner:</strong><br />
          • Miter Angle: <code class="font-bold text-blue-700">31.62&deg;</code><br />
          • Bevel Angle: <code class="font-bold text-indigo-700">33.86&deg; (Tilt Left)</code>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-3 rounded-lg border border-blue-200">
          <strong>135&deg; Bay Window Corner:</strong><br />
          • Miter Angle: <code class="font-bold text-blue-700">18.59&deg;</code><br />
          • Bevel Angle: <code class="font-bold text-indigo-700">22.95&deg; (Tilt Left)</code>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-blue-200 flex justify-between items-center">
        <span class="text-xs text-blue-700 font-medium">Need custom wall angles (e.g. 89.2° or 91.5°)?</span>
        <a href="/calculators/crown-molding" class="inline-flex items-center text-xs font-bold text-blue-800 hover:text-blue-900 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-blue-300 shadow-2xs">
          Open Interactive Crown Molding Calculator →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The 4 Cut Setup Matrix -->
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">The 4 Cut Positions (Molding Laying Face Up on Saw Table)</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8">
      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-blue-900 mb-2">1. Inside Corner — Left Piece</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-2"><strong>Miter:</strong> Turn Saw Table RIGHT to 31.6°</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-2"><strong>Bevel:</strong> Tilt Blade LEFT to 33.9°</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-700 font-medium">Position: Top of molding pressed against fence. Save the right end of the cut.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-blue-900 mb-2">2. Inside Corner — Right Piece</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-2"><strong>Miter:</strong> Turn Saw Table LEFT to 31.6°</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-2"><strong>Bevel:</strong> Tilt Blade LEFT to 33.9°</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-700 font-medium">Position: Bottom of molding against fence. Save the right end of the cut.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-900 mb-2">3. Outside Corner — Left Piece</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-2"><strong>Miter:</strong> Turn Saw Table LEFT to 31.6°</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-2"><strong>Bevel:</strong> Tilt Blade LEFT to 33.9°</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-700 font-medium">Position: Bottom of molding against fence. Save the left end of the cut.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-900 mb-2">4. Outside Corner — Right Piece</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-2"><strong>Miter:</strong> Turn Saw Table RIGHT to 31.6°</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-2"><strong>Bevel:</strong> Tilt Blade LEFT to 33.9°</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-700 font-medium">Position: Top of molding against fence. Save the left end of the cut.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Tools Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6 mb-8">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Related Carpentry &amp; Millwork Calculators</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
        <a href="/calculators/crown-molding" class="bg-white p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
          <div class="font-bold text-sm text-gray-900">Crown Molding Calculator</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Interactive compound angle dial &amp; board footage takeoff.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/calculators/trim-molding" class="bg-white p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
          <div class="font-bold text-sm text-gray-900">Baseboard Trim Calculator</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Calculate linear feet, corner miters &amp; waste.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/calculators/compound-miter" class="bg-white p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
          <div class="font-bold text-sm text-gray-900">Compound Miter Calculator</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Calculate bevel and miter cuts for custom shadowboxes.</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
